/E (Schizophrenia is a chronic and severe mental disorder that affects how a person thinks, feels and behaves. There is no medical test to diagnose schizophrenia. It is characterised by delusions, hallucinations, disorganized speech and behaviour and other symptoms that cause social or occupational dysfunction. People with schizophrenia may seem like they have lost touch with reality. The symptoms can be very disabling. )
